# Packeteer default-route ranking for RouterOS 7. Generated for review: nothing is applied.
# Check the commands against your RouterOS release first.
# Providers ranked by volume-weighted measured quality, lower score first. The order changes
# only past a 25% margin and then holds for 15m0s.
# Every default keeps suppress-hw-offload=yes: misses go to the CPU, backups included.
# Packeteer never changes a default route, its distance or its local-pref.

# 1. transit-b via 192.0.2.2: score 12.00, loss 0.10%, rtt 18.0 ms (now distance 5)
/ip route set [find dst-address=0.0.0.0/0 gateway=192.0.2.2] distance=1 suppress-hw-offload=yes

# 2. transit-c via 192.0.2.3: score 20.25, loss 0.50%, rtt 30.0 ms (now distance 2)
/ip route set [find dst-address=0.0.0.0/0 gateway=192.0.2.3] distance=2 suppress-hw-offload=yes

# 3. transit-a via 192.0.2.1: score 42.50, loss 1.25%, rtt 61.5 ms (now distance 1)
/ip route set [find dst-address=0.0.0.0/0 gateway=192.0.2.1] distance=3 suppress-hw-offload=yes

# 3. transit-a via 2001:db8::1: score 42.50, loss 1.25%, rtt 61.5 ms (now distance 1)
/ipv6 route set [find dst-address=::/0 gateway=2001:db8::1] distance=3 suppress-hw-offload=yes
